Nielstron compressed and tightened quasi-Riemann formalization, 2026-10-09.
Human contribution: Nielstron. AI-assisted research, proof compression,
certificate arithmetic, and formalization.

This is a derivative of Tim Gehrunger / ProofCouncil's QRH development in
gtimg/QuasiRiemannTracker at 290d9c5463344c3e2fab93b878f3281e77e3fd6f,
which builds on OpenAI/math at fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb,
Mathlib, and the dependencies identified in compressed/audit/dependency-licenses.json.
The original notices and source headers are retained. UPSTREAM-NOTICE is the
tracker's supplied notice. New and modified Lean sources remain Apache-2.0.

Modifications include shared binder contexts, shorter arithmetic proofs,
removal of unused helper declarations, readable zero-bound corollaries,
recomputed exact rational certificate coefficients and slack denominators,
and the added tighter-bound targets. The per-file baseline/final hashes and
token counts identify the changed source files in compressed/audit/token-counts.json.
compression.patch records the source differences from the pinned baseline.
The accepted manuscript under compressed/inputs is inherited unchanged and
describes the earlier proof; it is not presented as a newly authored manuscript.

The LeanLeanBench tokenizer is fetched from eth-sri/lean-lean at the pinned
revision recorded in the metric report; its source is not redistributed here.
No upstream author or checker project is represented as endorsing this result.
